WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.235
That evening Robin and his men returned to Sherwood Forest with Sir Richard.

2
00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:11.140
Little John had also found some guests.

3
00:00:11.141 --> 00:00:13.974
Robin grinned when he recognized the men.

4
00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:19.236
"Why, it's the Bishop of Hereford and three friars!" he said.

5
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:23.988
"Welcome, Bishop! I haven't seen you since Alan of Dale's wedding."

6
00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:27.440
The bishop paced nervously beneath a tree.

7
00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:29.928
He scowled but didn't say anything.

8
00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.097
He didn't want to join Robin's men for a feast.

9
00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:36.837
"Look at the bishop's horses, Robin," said Little John.

10
00:00:36.838 --> 00:00:38.505
Robin looked over.

11
00:00:38.506 --> 00:00:41.927
Six horses were tied to nearby trees.

12
00:00:41.928 --> 00:00:46.766
Five of them were loaded down with boxes and packs.

13
00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:49.722
Robin's eyes lit up eagerly.

14
00:00:49.723 --> 00:00:52.646
"We'll examine your treasures later, Bishop.

15
00:00:52.647 --> 00:00:55.637
But first I'd like you to meet another guest.

16
00:00:55.638 --> 00:00:58.748
This is Sir Richard."

17
00:00:58.749 --> 00:01:03.060
The bishop scowled again. "Sir Richard," he snapped.

18
00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:06.843
"I fear that we are companions in this den of . . ."

19
00:01:06.844 --> 00:01:11.884
His words trailed off as he shot an uneasy look at Robin.

20
00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:16.391
"Ha-ha!" Robin roared with laughter.

21
00:01:16.392 --> 00:01:19.972
"Go ahead, Bishop. We won't be insulted.

22
00:01:19.973 --> 00:01:23.275
You were about to say 'den of thieves.'"

23
00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:26.620
Sir Richard laughed, but the bishop did not.

24
00:01:26.621 --> 00:01:31.780
Some of Robin's men went to make fires for roasting meat.

25
00:01:31.781 --> 00:01:36.346
"We should entertain our guests while we wait for dinner," said Robin.

26
00:01:36.347 --> 00:01:39.701
"Let's have an archery contest and some music."

27
00:01:39.702 --> 00:01:44.276
Targets were set up and several men began to shoot.

28
00:01:44.277 --> 00:01:49.145
After the archery contest, a minstrel sang and played the harp.

29
00:01:49.146 --> 00:01:54.968
Meanwhile Robin talked and joked so pleasantly that Sir Richard forgot his troubles.

30
00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:59.216
And the bishop almost forgot his anger.

31
00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:03.117
At last two men came to say that the meal was ready.

32
00:02:03.118 --> 00:02:08.558
There was plenty of good food, and the feast lasted for hours.

33
00:02:08.559 --> 00:02:14.291
When everyone had finished eating, Robin told Sir Richard's sad story to the bishop.

34
00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:17.435
"You're the richest bishop in England," Robin said.

35
00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:19.596
"What can you do to help him?"

36
00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:21.942
The bishop said nothing.

37
00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:25.843
Instead he stared at the ground with a dark expression.

38
00:02:25.844 --> 00:02:28.023
"Little John!" called Robin.

39
00:02:28.024 --> 00:02:32.565
"It's time to see what the bishop's horses are carrying."

40
00:02:32.566 --> 00:02:35.473
Some men began opening the packs.

41
00:02:35.474 --> 00:02:40.427
The bishop's first horse was carrying silk for a merchant named Quentin.

42
00:02:40.428 --> 00:02:43.334
"I know Quentin," said Robin.

43
00:02:43.335 --> 00:02:47.004
"He's an honest man, so we won't touch his fabric."

44
00:02:47.005 --> 00:02:51.517
The horse's packs also held candles and velvet for a chapel.

45
00:02:51.518 --> 00:02:54.312
"We won't touch the candles either," said Robin.

46
00:02:54.313 --> 00:02:56.200
"They belong in the chapel.

47
00:02:56.201 --> 00:02:59.286
But priests don't need so much velvet.

48
00:02:59.287 --> 00:03:05.760
Divide it into three parts: one to be sold for charity, one for us, and one for the chapel."

49
00:03:05.761 --> 00:03:09.556
Robin examined every item the horses were carrying.

50
00:03:09.557 --> 00:03:12.259
Robin's men repacked some things.

51
00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.980
But they divided others into three parts.

52
00:03:15.981 --> 00:03:19.328
The last horse was led before Robin.

53
00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:22.516
"Now what is this one carrying?" he asked.

54
00:03:22.517 --> 00:03:27.331
"This horse has a box owned by the bishop," said Little John.

55
00:03:27.332 --> 00:03:31.277
"Bishop, do you have the key?" Robin asked.

56
00:03:31.278 --> 00:03:37.060
The bishop trembled as if he had the chills and shook his head. "No."

57
00:03:37.061 --> 00:03:42.065
"Will Scarlet, break open this box!" said Robin.

58
00:03:42.066 --> 00:03:48.274
Will struck the box several times with a huge sword and it finally sprang open.

59
00:03:48.275 --> 00:03:53.867
Robin's men gasped as a large heap of gold rolled out.

60
00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:58.405
Robin ordered Will Scarlet and Little John to count it.

61
00:03:58.406 --> 00:04:01.380
Much later Will called out the total.

62
00:04:01.381 --> 00:04:05.297
"Fifteen hundred pounds in gold coins!"

63
00:04:05.298 --> 00:04:07.110
Robin turned to the bishop.

64
00:04:07.111 --> 00:04:12.014
"Where did all this money come from?" he asked.

65
00:04:12.015 --> 00:04:16.292
"From collecting rents and fines," said a friar.

66
00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:20.946
The bishop glared at him for answering.

67
00:04:20.947 --> 00:04:27.302
"I'll let you keep five hundred pounds, which I hope you'll give to charity," said Robin to the bishop.

68
00:04:27.303 --> 00:04:30.590
"We'll keep five hundred pounds as payment for our feast.

69
00:04:30.591 --> 00:04:32.863
And Sir Richard will get the rest."

70
00:04:32.864 --> 00:04:38.021
Sir Richard looked astonished. "That's more than I need!" he said.

71
00:04:38.022 --> 00:04:42.823
"I thank you from the bottom of my heart, and I'll repay you one day."

72
00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:46.161
"That's not necessary," said Robin.

73
00:04:46.162 --> 00:04:49.724
The bishop was grateful that Robin didn't take everything.

74
00:04:49.725 --> 00:04:52.186
Sir Richard mounted his horse.

75
00:04:52.187 --> 00:04:57.622
"I must go for my wife will be anxious about my whereabouts."

76
00:04:57.623 --> 00:05:03.616
The bishop tried to leave too. "It's getting late. I must go as well."

77
00:05:03.617 --> 00:05:09.927
"Oh, no," said Robin. "You're our guest until Sir Richard pays his debt.

78
00:05:09.928 --> 00:05:12.348
I don't want you interfering with that.

79
00:05:12.349 --> 00:05:16.444
But don't worry. We'll treat you well."

80
00:05:16.445 --> 00:05:20.959
So Robin fed and entertained the bishop for three days.

81
00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.582
The bishop had such fun that sometimes he forgot he was a prisoner.

82
00:05:26.583 --> 00:05:32.950
But when he finally left, he said to the friars, "Robin will regret the way he treated us.

83
00:05:32.951 --> 00:05:37.780
I'll make sure of that."

